  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Constellation="AQR" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="-15.284723613073389" Magnitude="0" Name="R Aquarii" Opacity="100" RA="23.73051846113259" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/hst/heic2413a/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="0.26094591291500124">
    <Description>This image features R Aquarii, a symbiotic binary star that lies only roughly 1,000 light-years from Earth in the constellation Aquarius. This is a type of binary star system consisting of a white dwarf and a red giant that is surrounded by a large, dynamic nebula. [Image description: A bright binary star surrounded by a nebula. The star, in the centre, is a large white spot surrounded by a circular glow. It has a large, X-shaped set of diffraction spikes around it. The nebula extends far above, below, left and right of the star in long, arcing shapes made of thin, multicoloured filaments — mostly red and greenish colours, but lit in a bright cyan near the star where its light illuminates the gas.]</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet BandPass="Visible" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.04493468785944259" BaseTileLevel="0" BottomsUp="False" CenterX="355.9577833071252" CenterY="-15.284718903669555" DataSetType="Sky" ElevationModel="False" FileType=".png" Generic="False" Name="R Aquarii" OffsetX="1.0970382778184225e-05" OffsetY="5.485191389092113e-06" Projection="Tan" QuadTreeMap="" Rotation="-82.37999999999978" Sparse="True" StockSet="False" TileLevels="4" Url="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/hst/heic2413a/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" WidthFactor="2" Xcorepipe_ids="hst|heic2413a">
        <Credits>NASA, ESA, M. Stute, M. Karovska, D. de Martin &amp; M. Zamani (ESA/Hubble)</Credits>
        <CreditsUrl>https://esahubble.org/images/heic2413a/</CreditsUrl>
        <ThumbnailUrl>https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/hst/heic2413a/thumb.jpg</ThumbnailUrl>
